1
00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:03,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

2
00:00:04,109 --> 00:00:06,111
[♪ opening theme music playing]

3
00:00:40,646 --> 00:00:44,066
FLEX X COP 2

4
00:00:44,149 --> 00:00:46,902
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

5
00:00:46,985 --> 00:00:49,071
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

6
00:00:54,618 --> 00:00:56,078
[panting]

7
00:00:56,161 --> 00:00:58,121
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

8
00:00:59,456 --> 00:01:00,624
[grunts, panting]

9
00:01:04,461 --> 00:01:05,796
[exhales, panting]

10
00:01:12,135 --> 00:01:13,762
[continues panting] Oh, oh...

11
00:01:16,431 --> 00:01:17,683
[Isoo continues panting]

12
00:01:21,103 --> 00:01:22,604
Kid, go inside.

13
00:01:22,688 --> 00:01:24,064
Go inside!

14
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:27,442
[exhales anxiously]

15
00:01:29,695 --> 00:01:30,904
Your heart's pounding.

16
00:01:30,987 --> 00:01:32,114
[kid breathing shakily]

17
00:01:32,698 --> 00:01:34,449
[♪ music increases in tempo]

18
00:01:37,160 --> 00:01:39,496
Drop the knife.
There's nowhere left to run.

19
00:01:39,579 --> 00:01:40,580
Should I kill him?

20
00:01:42,916 --> 00:01:44,334
[Pilgu] Drop it.

21
00:01:44,418 --> 00:01:45,961
I'll slice his neck.

22
00:01:46,044 --> 00:01:47,254
[Hyera] Fine.

23
00:01:47,337 --> 00:01:48,588
Calm down.

24
00:01:48,672 --> 00:01:49,673
[Pilgu] Put it down.

25
00:01:53,718 --> 00:01:54,845
Get back.

26
00:01:58,974 --> 00:02:00,016
Drop it.

27
00:02:00,559 --> 00:02:01,768
Drop it, you bastards!

28
00:02:01,852 --> 00:02:03,061
[kid panting frantically]

29
00:02:05,897 --> 00:02:07,607
I said, drop it, you bastards!

30
00:02:07,691 --> 00:02:08,775
[taser fires, crackling]

31
00:02:08,859 --> 00:02:10,318
[grunting, convulsing]

32
00:02:14,698 --> 00:02:16,867
[♪ upbeat swing jazz music playing]

33
00:02:16,950 --> 00:02:18,702
[mimics gunshot] You're no big deal.

34
00:02:21,705 --> 00:02:22,831
[grunting]

35
00:02:23,623 --> 00:02:25,000
[siren blaring]

36
00:02:31,548 --> 00:02:33,842
[Taegyun] What's going on?
What's the case?

37
00:02:33,925 --> 00:02:35,093
EPISODE 12

38
00:02:35,177 --> 00:02:37,721
This is the real killer
who set Detective Jin up.

39
00:02:37,804 --> 00:02:39,264
What are you talking about?

40
00:02:40,849 --> 00:02:42,851
Sir! It's been a while.

41
00:02:42,934 --> 00:02:44,019
Wait, he's...

42
00:02:44,102 --> 00:02:46,271
Detective Jin, when did you get out?

43
00:02:46,354 --> 00:02:47,522
Yesterday.

44
00:02:48,774 --> 00:02:50,817
I was kind of hurt.

45
00:02:50,901 --> 00:02:52,527
What was it you said to me?

46
00:02:53,195 --> 00:02:55,530
[mimicking Taegyun]
"A goddamn detective killed someone?"

47
00:02:55,614 --> 00:02:58,283
How could you say that to me?

48
00:02:58,366 --> 00:03:01,077
I liked you, sir, but you've let me down.

49
00:03:01,161 --> 00:03:02,662
[Isoo swears softly]

50
00:03:02,746 --> 00:03:04,664
[huffs] Let's go.

51
00:03:06,750 --> 00:03:08,001
[Taegyun] Hey...

52
00:03:08,084 --> 00:03:12,088
He won't try to get back at me, will he?

53
00:03:12,506 --> 00:03:16,343
Oh, this is bad, sir.
He doesn't really let things go.

54
00:03:16,426 --> 00:03:17,928
I think he'll try to get revenge.

55
00:03:18,011 --> 00:03:19,763
This could get really ugly.

56
00:03:19,846 --> 00:03:21,181
Goodness.

57
00:03:21,890 --> 00:03:23,308
-Honestly, that punk.
-[♪ music fades]

58
00:03:36,071 --> 00:03:37,405
You did this, didn't you?

59
00:03:37,489 --> 00:03:38,907
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

60
00:03:40,575 --> 00:03:42,786
Kim Younghwan drugged me unconscious...

61
00:03:45,330 --> 00:03:46,373
<i>then let you inside.</i>

62
00:03:49,834 --> 00:03:51,336
What were you two trying to do?

63
00:03:54,756 --> 00:03:56,341
Why did you kill Younghwan?

64
00:03:58,969 --> 00:04:01,680
We found a bag containing
50 million won inside your house.

65
00:04:03,557 --> 00:04:05,725
FORENSIC INVESTIGATION
POLICE

66
00:04:05,809 --> 00:04:07,435
[camera shutter clicking]

67
00:04:09,854 --> 00:04:10,897
Where did you get it?

68
00:04:14,359 --> 00:04:15,735
[yawns]

69
00:04:20,115 --> 00:04:21,533
We found your car, too.

70
00:04:24,744 --> 00:04:26,746
<i>You took the subway from the scene,</i>

71
00:04:28,290 --> 00:04:30,542
<i>then got into your car</i>
<i>at a public parking lot.</i>

72
00:04:35,463 --> 00:04:36,756
[camera shutter clicking]

73
00:04:36,840 --> 00:04:38,925
[♪ music swells, fades]

74
00:04:39,593 --> 00:04:41,261
We're investigating it right now.

75
00:04:41,344 --> 00:04:42,721
We'll find evidence soon.

76
00:04:44,347 --> 00:04:45,390
Just come clean.

77
00:04:47,934 --> 00:04:48,977
[clears throat]

78
00:04:54,649 --> 00:04:55,901
I want to call my lawyer.

79
00:04:59,154 --> 00:05:00,280
I want my phone call.

80
00:05:00,363 --> 00:05:02,073
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

81
00:05:26,765 --> 00:05:28,350
[cell phone vibrating]

82
00:05:35,357 --> 00:05:37,067
[cell phone continues vibrating]

83
00:05:38,109 --> 00:05:39,235
[exhales softly]

84
00:05:41,988 --> 00:05:43,073
Mr. Lawyer.

85
00:05:44,157 --> 00:05:45,533
I've been caught.

86
00:05:47,786 --> 00:05:49,120
You're not very skilled.

87
00:05:49,204 --> 00:05:51,331
Of course, I know you well, Mr. Lawyer.

88
00:05:52,123 --> 00:05:54,376
I know exactly who you are.

89
00:05:56,169 --> 00:05:57,712
You know me?

90
00:05:57,796 --> 00:05:59,589
You're famous.

91
00:06:00,340 --> 00:06:03,969
I'm more thorough than you think.

92
00:06:04,678 --> 00:06:06,471
Then why did you get caught?

93
00:06:07,514 --> 00:06:08,765
Uh...

94
00:06:10,767 --> 00:06:12,602
I was unlucky.

95
00:06:14,396 --> 00:06:17,357
In any case,
you'll have to come down here.

96
00:06:18,274 --> 00:06:20,527
I'll send you a lawyer,
so don't say anything.

97
00:06:22,237 --> 00:06:23,989
[whispering] You'd better hurry.

98
00:06:24,614 --> 00:06:25,949
I'm...

99
00:06:28,576 --> 00:06:30,370
not very patient.

100
00:06:40,964 --> 00:06:42,090
[♪ music fades]

101
00:06:42,799 --> 00:06:45,010
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

102
00:06:46,928 --> 00:06:48,346
GRUDGE, ACCOMPLICE?

103
00:06:48,430 --> 00:06:50,056
HOLDS DEEP GRUDGE AGAINST JIN ISOO

104
00:06:53,977 --> 00:06:55,603
FOUR STABS TO CHEST, ABDOMEN, BACK

105
00:06:58,481 --> 00:06:59,482
Did you find anything?

106
00:06:59,566 --> 00:07:01,818
There's nothing at the house
but the cash bag.

107
00:07:01,901 --> 00:07:04,612
Blood was found on the steering wheel.

108
00:07:05,488 --> 00:07:07,532
They're checking it
against Kim Younghwan's DNA.

109
00:07:08,992 --> 00:07:10,201
That's not enough.

110
00:07:12,746 --> 00:07:14,706
You stabbed Kim Younghwan

111
00:07:14,789 --> 00:07:17,167
and he went in there to save him.

112
00:07:17,250 --> 00:07:18,376
That makes sense, too.

113
00:07:18,460 --> 00:07:20,336
Isn't there a way to make him confess?

114
00:07:20,420 --> 00:07:22,714
He said he won't talk without a lawyer.

115
00:07:22,797 --> 00:07:25,550
[scoffs softly] With four convictions,
he knows how this works.

116
00:07:26,676 --> 00:07:29,262
But I can't see the bigger picture.

117
00:07:29,888 --> 00:07:31,681
Someone gave him that money to do this.

118
00:07:32,766 --> 00:07:33,933
Who could it be?

119
00:07:34,017 --> 00:07:36,686
Maybe he was called in to kill you,
then things went wrong.

120
00:07:37,395 --> 00:07:40,398
No, that's not what Younghwan said.

121
00:07:40,482 --> 00:07:43,234
What would happen

122
00:07:43,318 --> 00:07:46,446
if the great Jin Isoo ended up in prison?

123
00:07:47,489 --> 00:07:50,200
He wanted you to get arrested for murder?

124
00:07:50,283 --> 00:07:53,828
Like that case where he was the suspect?

125
00:07:54,579 --> 00:07:55,580
Mmm?

126
00:07:56,247 --> 00:07:59,334
He was the initial suspect
in the murder of actress Han Yura.

127
00:08:00,210 --> 00:08:03,338
<i>He fell asleep after taking drugs,</i>
<i>and there was blood on his clothes.</i>

128
00:08:03,421 --> 00:08:04,881
[♪ music increases in tempo]

129
00:08:09,969 --> 00:08:10,970
Then,

130
00:08:12,013 --> 00:08:13,848
he ordered Cho Pilgu to kill him?

131
00:08:13,932 --> 00:08:15,558
To send Isoo to prison?

132
00:08:15,642 --> 00:08:18,436
I don't think anyone would go that far.

133
00:08:23,566 --> 00:08:25,401
KIM YOUNGHWAN, CHO PILGU
ACCOMPLICE?

134
00:08:27,570 --> 00:08:29,405
For now, let's look into Cho Pilgu.

135
00:08:29,489 --> 00:08:32,075
See if there's a way to make him confess.

136
00:08:32,158 --> 00:08:34,327
Did you bring back Cho Pilgu's computer?

137
00:08:34,410 --> 00:08:36,079
Yes, Forensics is going through it.

138
00:08:36,162 --> 00:08:37,705
[♪ music swells, fades]

139
00:08:37,789 --> 00:08:39,582
[sighs deeply]

140
00:08:40,959 --> 00:08:42,877
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

141
00:08:57,767 --> 00:08:59,435
YU SEONGWON
STUDIO

142
00:09:01,020 --> 00:09:02,856
[♪ music increases in tempo]

143
00:09:18,121 --> 00:09:20,248
YU SEONGWON

144
00:09:26,087 --> 00:09:27,088
[♪ music fades]

145
00:09:29,966 --> 00:09:30,967
[door closes]

146
00:09:33,303 --> 00:09:34,804
Are you two sleeping together?

147
00:09:34,888 --> 00:09:36,014
Don't you know how to knock?

148
00:09:37,015 --> 00:09:39,058
I wasn't really brought up properly.

149
00:09:39,142 --> 00:09:40,643
At least I got a good show.

150
00:09:41,686 --> 00:09:42,729
What do you want?

151
00:09:44,314 --> 00:09:45,857
For you to be a mother for once.

152
00:09:46,691 --> 00:09:47,692
Actually,

153
00:09:48,401 --> 00:09:51,779
this is more important for you in the end.

154
00:09:51,863 --> 00:09:55,033
You know Hansu Group's
Jin Isoo got arrested, right?

155
00:09:56,367 --> 00:09:57,619
He was released yesterday.

156
00:09:59,329 --> 00:10:00,413
That was my doing.

157
00:10:00,496 --> 00:10:02,207
[♪ tense, ominous music playing]

158
00:10:03,166 --> 00:10:04,167
[sighs softly]

159
00:10:05,919 --> 00:10:07,545
4 WEEKS BEFORE KIM YOUNGHWAN'S DEATH

160
00:10:07,629 --> 00:10:08,880
Thank you for your time.

161
00:10:08,963 --> 00:10:10,673
[Seongwon] Of course. Thank you.
[chuckles softly]

162
00:10:17,388 --> 00:10:18,389
[clears throat]

163
00:10:18,473 --> 00:10:19,766
[Younghwan] Hey, Seongwon.

164
00:10:21,809 --> 00:10:22,936
Congratulations.

165
00:10:26,731 --> 00:10:28,566
Hey, I'm hurt.

166
00:10:29,734 --> 00:10:31,653
It's me, Younghwan. Isoo's friend.

167
00:10:31,736 --> 00:10:34,739
We met a couple of times before.

168
00:10:37,158 --> 00:10:38,243
Ah.

169
00:10:38,785 --> 00:10:39,786
Right.

170
00:10:40,954 --> 00:10:43,081
-Here.
-Uh, thank you.

171
00:10:43,164 --> 00:10:44,332
[chuckles softly]

172
00:10:44,415 --> 00:10:45,750
[♪ music increases in tempo]

173
00:10:47,126 --> 00:10:48,586
Isoo was here yesterday.

174
00:10:52,465 --> 00:10:54,175
Uh... Really?

175
00:10:54,759 --> 00:10:56,094
[chuckles softly] Hey...

176
00:10:56,177 --> 00:10:58,471
Anyway, I'm impressed.

177
00:10:59,097 --> 00:11:01,474
You've become such a famous artist.

178
00:11:02,267 --> 00:11:03,518
Even I'm proud of you.

179
00:11:03,601 --> 00:11:04,727
[chuckles softly]

180
00:11:04,811 --> 00:11:07,355
How did you make all these amazing pieces?

181
00:11:07,438 --> 00:11:08,690
[chuckles]

182
00:11:10,650 --> 00:11:11,651
[inhales sharply]

183
00:11:11,734 --> 00:11:14,028
Anyway, the thing is,

184
00:11:14,654 --> 00:11:16,030
there's something I want to discuss.

185
00:11:17,407 --> 00:11:19,409
Can I visit you at your studio sometime?

186
00:11:21,661 --> 00:11:23,663
Of course. Feel free to come.

187
00:11:25,373 --> 00:11:26,374
Okay.

188
00:11:27,250 --> 00:11:28,251
I'll call you soon.

189
00:11:30,169 --> 00:11:31,170
Congratulations again.

190
00:11:31,254 --> 00:11:33,131
[♪ ominous, ticking music playing]

191
00:11:35,842 --> 00:11:36,968
[scoffs softly]

192
00:11:39,220 --> 00:11:41,472
He's like a dog without its master.

193
00:11:41,556 --> 00:11:42,724
[♪ music swells, fades]

194
00:11:45,727 --> 00:11:47,645
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

195
00:11:47,729 --> 00:11:49,105
[exhales contentedly]

196
00:11:49,689 --> 00:11:51,899
[exhales] Even the whiskey you drink
is good.

197
00:11:53,484 --> 00:11:54,819
This is the one Isoo made.

198
00:11:55,361 --> 00:11:56,362
Never tried it before?

199
00:12:00,575 --> 00:12:01,909
Uh... [chuckles nervously]

200
00:12:02,660 --> 00:12:04,203
No. [scoffs]

201
00:12:04,287 --> 00:12:05,288
[scoffs softly]

202
00:12:06,497 --> 00:12:08,624
Anyway... [sighs]

203
00:12:08,708 --> 00:12:12,670
...shouldn't you start thinking about
selling your pieces now?

204
00:12:12,754 --> 00:12:13,880
Mmm.

205
00:12:15,757 --> 00:12:17,258
The thing is,

206
00:12:18,259 --> 00:12:23,639
I'm well-connected with
chaebols, celebrities, and big spenders.

207
00:12:25,224 --> 00:12:27,852
People are already lining up
to buy your work.

208
00:12:28,978 --> 00:12:30,313
Really?

209
00:12:30,396 --> 00:12:33,066
You have no idea.
Right now, they keep calling me

210
00:12:33,149 --> 00:12:36,277
to ask if they can buy your work.
[chuckling]

211
00:12:36,944 --> 00:12:37,945
So, how about it?

212
00:12:38,780 --> 00:12:42,909
Should I take this chance
and become your art dealer?

213
00:12:45,453 --> 00:12:47,038
Uh, don't get me wrong. [chuckles]

214
00:12:47,121 --> 00:12:50,083
I'm not trying to use this
to make money or anything like that.

215
00:12:50,958 --> 00:12:52,585
Your work is just too good.

216
00:12:53,503 --> 00:12:54,962
You run a production company.

217
00:12:56,381 --> 00:12:57,507
[chuckles nervously]

218
00:12:58,299 --> 00:12:59,801
Yeah, well,

219
00:13:00,551 --> 00:13:01,928
I'm thinking of quitting.

220
00:13:03,429 --> 00:13:04,972
So the rumors were true.

221
00:13:05,723 --> 00:13:06,808
Mmm?

222
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:09,936
I heard you went to prison
for doing drugs.

223
00:13:14,607 --> 00:13:17,235
-[sighs wearily]
-Why didn't Isoo help you back then?

224
00:13:17,944 --> 00:13:19,320
Is that why you two fell out?

225
00:13:22,156 --> 00:13:23,157
No.

226
00:13:25,326 --> 00:13:26,994
That bastard turned me in.

227
00:13:27,078 --> 00:13:28,871
[♪ suspenseful, pulsating music playing]

228
00:13:28,955 --> 00:13:30,331
Uh...

229
00:13:30,415 --> 00:13:31,582
Isoo did that?

230
00:13:32,542 --> 00:13:35,128
Yeah. He was supposed to be my friend.

231
00:13:35,545 --> 00:13:36,546
Uh...

232
00:13:36,629 --> 00:13:37,630
But why?

233
00:13:37,713 --> 00:13:40,842
He thinks he's a detective now. [scoffs]

234
00:13:42,677 --> 00:13:47,473
Isoo thinks of himself as a detective?

235
00:13:47,557 --> 00:13:50,393
That's why he sold out his own friend.

236
00:13:52,895 --> 00:13:54,397
Are you just going to take that?

237
00:13:55,314 --> 00:13:57,275
Actually, I was so pissed off,

238
00:13:57,358 --> 00:14:00,778
I snuck into his house
and thought about killing him.

239
00:14:01,654 --> 00:14:02,655
You snuck in?

240
00:14:04,490 --> 00:14:06,450
I have a key to his house.

241
00:14:08,870 --> 00:14:10,913
How about we mess with Isoo a little?

242
00:14:11,831 --> 00:14:12,832
How?

243
00:14:12,915 --> 00:14:14,375
[♪ music turns ominous]

244
00:14:15,751 --> 00:14:17,378
Let's get him locked up for drugs, too.

245
00:14:18,004 --> 00:14:20,590
You go inside
and make him take drugs somehow,

246
00:14:20,673 --> 00:14:22,508
then I'll send someone.

247
00:14:22,592 --> 00:14:25,761
He'll put Isoo in a car
and make him cause an accident.

248
00:14:27,221 --> 00:14:29,473
I think it could become a huge scandal.

249
00:14:29,557 --> 00:14:30,933
[laughs maliciously]

250
00:14:31,017 --> 00:14:32,476
It's going to be so much fun.

251
00:14:33,477 --> 00:14:34,520
[chuckles nervously]

252
00:14:36,022 --> 00:14:37,023
Uh...

253
00:14:37,106 --> 00:14:38,900
Aren't you close with Isoo?

254
00:14:38,983 --> 00:14:40,109
Why would you do that?

255
00:14:40,193 --> 00:14:42,528
He kind of screwed me over.

256
00:14:44,530 --> 00:14:47,325
It's fine. It's just a joke.

257
00:14:47,408 --> 00:14:50,203
Isoo will be able to get out of it anyway.

258
00:14:50,286 --> 00:14:51,621
And you can just move abroad,

259
00:14:52,246 --> 00:14:53,414
as my art dealer.

260
00:14:57,376 --> 00:14:58,419
[chuckles nervously]

261
00:14:58,502 --> 00:14:59,962
[♪ music increases in tempo]

262
00:15:07,720 --> 00:15:09,388
Find someone.

263
00:15:10,431 --> 00:15:11,807
I need a job done.

264
00:15:11,891 --> 00:15:12,975
Understood.

265
00:15:14,602 --> 00:15:16,812
Are you saying
you gave the order to kill him?

266
00:15:16,896 --> 00:15:18,940
-Yes.
-Why?

267
00:15:19,023 --> 00:15:20,024
[♪ music fades]

268
00:15:20,107 --> 00:15:22,109
Just because. I thought it'd be fun.

269
00:15:23,236 --> 00:15:24,278
[scoffs]

270
00:15:25,821 --> 00:15:27,323
[breathes deeply]

271
00:15:27,406 --> 00:15:28,407
But

272
00:15:29,116 --> 00:15:31,160
I think he found out who I am.

273
00:15:31,244 --> 00:15:32,495
[♪ tense music playing]

274
00:15:32,578 --> 00:15:35,206
How? You said Mr. Hwang hired him.

275
00:15:35,289 --> 00:15:36,290
Yeah.

276
00:15:36,374 --> 00:15:37,875
Mr. Hwang dropped off the money.

277
00:15:38,417 --> 00:15:40,336
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

278
00:15:41,128 --> 00:15:42,546
[keypad beeping]

279
00:16:00,564 --> 00:16:01,649
<i>He must've followed him.</i>

280
00:16:17,957 --> 00:16:19,333
[♪ music turns ominous]

281
00:16:21,043 --> 00:16:22,044
You...

282
00:16:24,046 --> 00:16:25,339
Why do you...

283
00:16:27,133 --> 00:16:28,884
keep doing this?

284
00:16:28,968 --> 00:16:31,178
It's a bit too late to ask that.

285
00:16:32,179 --> 00:16:35,474
You should've asked when I was nine,
before you had me committed.

286
00:16:43,899 --> 00:16:44,900
You might...

287
00:16:46,360 --> 00:16:48,112
want to hurry.

288
00:16:48,195 --> 00:16:49,947
If he decides to talk,

289
00:16:51,073 --> 00:16:52,283
me,

290
00:16:52,867 --> 00:16:53,868
you,

291
00:16:53,951 --> 00:16:55,953
and this company you love so much

292
00:16:57,538 --> 00:16:59,123
will be over.

293
00:17:07,465 --> 00:17:08,549
[door opens]

294
00:17:09,800 --> 00:17:10,843
[door slams]

295
00:17:12,428 --> 00:17:13,429
[clink]

296
00:17:13,512 --> 00:17:15,639
[screams in frustration]

297
00:17:15,723 --> 00:17:17,350
[breathing heavily]

298
00:17:17,433 --> 00:17:18,517
[sighs in exasperation]

299
00:17:20,019 --> 00:17:21,854
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

300
00:17:46,379 --> 00:17:47,588
[♪ music fades]

301
00:17:50,466 --> 00:17:53,052
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

302
00:17:58,057 --> 00:17:59,225
I'm Mr. Cho Pilgu's lawyer.

303
00:18:01,477 --> 00:18:02,478
Okay.

304
00:18:04,689 --> 00:18:05,898
[sighs in exasperation]

305
00:18:08,067 --> 00:18:09,860
Song Yeonwoo.

306
00:18:09,944 --> 00:18:12,863
First, please tell me what happened.

307
00:18:12,947 --> 00:18:14,532
[breathes deeply]

308
00:18:14,615 --> 00:18:17,201
There's nothing much to tell.

309
00:18:17,284 --> 00:18:18,285
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

310
00:18:18,369 --> 00:18:20,996
He opened the door for me, so I went in.

311
00:18:23,874 --> 00:18:25,668
You'll handle the rest, right?

312
00:18:28,045 --> 00:18:29,046
I'll leave you to it.

313
00:18:30,923 --> 00:18:32,049
[chuckles]

314
00:18:32,133 --> 00:18:33,300
Wait.

315
00:18:33,384 --> 00:18:34,427
What?

316
00:18:34,510 --> 00:18:36,387
That's not what I was told.

317
00:18:36,470 --> 00:18:37,680
What do you mean?

318
00:18:38,097 --> 00:18:39,265
-[squelch]
-[Younghwan grunts softly]

319
00:18:39,974 --> 00:18:41,267
-[squelch]
-[groans]

320
00:18:41,892 --> 00:18:43,018
-[squelch]
-[exclaims]

321
00:18:43,436 --> 00:18:45,271
-[groaning]
-[squelching]

322
00:18:45,354 --> 00:18:46,439
[exclaims]

323
00:18:46,522 --> 00:18:48,232
[♪ tense, ominous music playing]

324
00:18:49,316 --> 00:18:50,317
Come here.

325
00:18:50,401 --> 00:18:51,819
-[squelch]
-[groans]

326
00:19:06,208 --> 00:19:07,418
[exhales softly]

327
00:19:08,919 --> 00:19:10,004
[knife clatters]

328
00:19:12,840 --> 00:19:13,883
[Pilgu grunts]

329
00:19:13,966 --> 00:19:15,509
[♪ music increases in tempo]

330
00:19:16,510 --> 00:19:17,553
[grunts]

331
00:19:22,349 --> 00:19:23,350
[grunts]

332
00:19:25,770 --> 00:19:26,937
[grunts]

333
00:19:27,021 --> 00:19:28,439
[panting]

334
00:19:28,522 --> 00:19:29,899
[♪ music swells]

335
00:19:31,108 --> 00:19:32,318
[grunts]

336
00:19:33,110 --> 00:19:35,070
[grunts] He's even heavier.

337
00:19:35,154 --> 00:19:36,322
[♪ music resumes tempo]

338
00:19:36,405 --> 00:19:37,406
Any fingerprints?

339
00:19:38,449 --> 00:19:40,576
I was wearing gloves the whole time.

340
00:19:41,869 --> 00:19:42,995
We can build a story.

341
00:19:44,246 --> 00:19:46,415
The police don't have
any conclusive evidence.

342
00:19:47,541 --> 00:19:50,377
We'll say Kim Younghwan took you there
as his bodyguard.

343
00:19:50,461 --> 00:19:52,671
He was afraid Jin Isoo would kill him.

344
00:19:52,755 --> 00:19:55,216
You went up there
because he called you for help.

345
00:19:56,050 --> 00:19:57,301
That's how you got blood on you.

346
00:20:01,180 --> 00:20:02,598
We might be here a while.

347
00:20:03,390 --> 00:20:04,517
Why don't we eat something?

348
00:20:05,100 --> 00:20:06,143
[chuckles softly]

349
00:20:07,144 --> 00:20:08,479
-Sounds good.
-[♪ music fades]

350
00:20:11,065 --> 00:20:12,107
[slurps]

351
00:20:13,526 --> 00:20:14,944
Just stick to what we rehearsed.

352
00:20:15,027 --> 00:20:16,612
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

353
00:20:18,823 --> 00:20:19,824
And sign this.

354
00:20:22,576 --> 00:20:23,702
It's a retainer agreement.

355
00:20:23,786 --> 00:20:24,829
[sighs deeply]

356
00:20:24,912 --> 00:20:26,413
Such a hassle.

357
00:20:37,883 --> 00:20:39,009
[slurps]

358
00:20:41,595 --> 00:20:43,055
Expensive lawyers

359
00:20:44,598 --> 00:20:45,599
are worth it.

360
00:20:45,683 --> 00:20:47,101
Of course.

361
00:20:47,184 --> 00:20:48,185
[chuckles smugly]

362
00:20:48,269 --> 00:20:49,520
[slurping]

363
00:20:52,523 --> 00:20:53,649
Eat up.

364
00:20:55,901 --> 00:20:56,902
[slurping]

365
00:20:59,989 --> 00:21:02,741
INTERVIEW ROOM

366
00:21:02,825 --> 00:21:03,826
[♪ music fades]

367
00:21:10,416 --> 00:21:12,293
They probably worked out a story.

368
00:21:14,795 --> 00:21:17,756
Without more evidence,
we need to set Cho Pilgu free.

369
00:21:20,175 --> 00:21:21,468
[sighs heavily]

370
00:21:23,429 --> 00:21:24,430
Did you find anything?

371
00:21:24,513 --> 00:21:27,558
His computer records came back,
but there was nothing significant.

372
00:21:28,183 --> 00:21:30,436
Nothing on his phone either.

373
00:21:31,145 --> 00:21:32,146
Let me see.

374
00:21:35,399 --> 00:21:36,567
DIGITAL FORENSIC REPORT

375
00:21:41,530 --> 00:21:43,282
YU SEONGWON

376
00:21:43,365 --> 00:21:44,575
What's this?

377
00:21:44,658 --> 00:21:46,619
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

378
00:21:47,620 --> 00:21:50,122
He searched for Yu Seongwon online.

379
00:21:58,547 --> 00:21:59,840
[Isoo] It's Yu Seongwon's studio.

380
00:22:02,593 --> 00:22:04,511
Minjae installed another camera. Let's go.

381
00:22:04,595 --> 00:22:05,888
Okay.

382
00:22:05,971 --> 00:22:07,389
[♪ music increases in tempo]

383
00:22:10,309 --> 00:22:11,685
Look up Yu Seongwon.

384
00:22:11,769 --> 00:22:12,853
Okay.

385
00:22:13,604 --> 00:22:15,272
Did you hear anything about this?

386
00:22:15,356 --> 00:22:16,357
No, nothing.

387
00:22:20,319 --> 00:22:21,487
[line ringing]

388
00:22:23,989 --> 00:22:25,741
[automated voice]
<i>The number you have dialed...</i>

389
00:22:26,200 --> 00:22:28,160
-[line disconnects]
-He's not picking up.

390
00:22:28,243 --> 00:22:29,578
[♪ music swells]

391
00:22:32,081 --> 00:22:33,165
[sighs softly]

392
00:22:34,249 --> 00:22:35,626
-[cell phone vibrates]
-[♪ music fades]

393
00:22:35,709 --> 00:22:37,252
PI JEONG MINJAE

394
00:22:37,336 --> 00:22:39,755
[Minjae] <i>I can't pick up right now.</i>
<i>What is it?</i>

395
00:22:44,134 --> 00:22:46,512
[Hyera] <i>Did anything happen</i>
<i>with Yu Seongwon yesterday?</i>

396
00:22:50,265 --> 00:22:52,059
[Minjae] <i>He just went back to his studio.</i>

397
00:22:53,394 --> 00:22:54,395
[Hyera] <i>Where are you?</i>

398
00:22:57,856 --> 00:22:59,608
[Minjae] <i>I'm staking out</i>
<i>for a different case.</i>

399
00:23:00,484 --> 00:23:02,236
[breathes deeply]

400
00:23:04,905 --> 00:23:06,991
Does Yu Seongwon know Kim Younghwan?

401
00:23:07,074 --> 00:23:08,075
Yeah.

402
00:23:09,034 --> 00:23:10,703
He met him a few times with me.

403
00:23:11,537 --> 00:23:12,579
But why?

404
00:23:13,205 --> 00:23:16,000
I get why Younghwan
would want to get back at me,

405
00:23:17,292 --> 00:23:19,545
but what does Seongwon
have to do with this?

406
00:23:23,090 --> 00:23:24,174
[♪ music swells, fades]

407
00:23:28,053 --> 00:23:29,346
Do you know the passcode?

408
00:23:29,430 --> 00:23:32,266
Yeah, we know each other's,
just to be safe.

409
00:23:32,349 --> 00:23:33,559
[digital beeping]

410
00:23:39,815 --> 00:23:40,983
[sighs softly]

411
00:23:42,776 --> 00:23:44,361
That's the monitor for Yu Seongwon.

412
00:23:44,445 --> 00:23:45,696
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

413
00:23:45,779 --> 00:23:48,699
-Let's check the saved files first.
-Okay.

414
00:23:51,618 --> 00:23:53,078
[mouse clicking]

415
00:24:12,973 --> 00:24:13,974
[Isoo] Oh.

416
00:24:14,683 --> 00:24:15,684
That's Kim Younghwan.

417
00:24:21,273 --> 00:24:22,441
[doorbell chiming]

418
00:24:25,319 --> 00:24:27,279
Did they plan this together?

419
00:24:27,362 --> 00:24:30,032
Yu Seongwon might have
wanted revenge on you.

420
00:24:30,616 --> 00:24:33,285
He knows now that you suspect him.

421
00:24:33,368 --> 00:24:35,412
He tried to frame me for murder
because of that?

422
00:24:36,246 --> 00:24:37,289
Does that mean

423
00:24:38,373 --> 00:24:40,501
Younghwan told Seongwon to murder him?

424
00:24:42,002 --> 00:24:45,339
No, Kim Younghwan was
probably used as well.

425
00:24:45,422 --> 00:24:48,884
Cho Pilgu went to Yu Seongwon's studio,

426
00:24:48,967 --> 00:24:50,594
so Yu Seongwon must have hired him.

427
00:24:51,970 --> 00:24:53,764
The 50 million won was
payment for the murder.

428
00:24:53,847 --> 00:24:54,848
[♪ music fades]

429
00:24:54,932 --> 00:24:57,434
Kim Younghwan's plan was something else,

430
00:24:58,644 --> 00:25:01,772
but Yu Seongwon hired someone
to kill Kim Younghwan?

431
00:25:01,855 --> 00:25:03,440
[♪ somber, suspenseful music playing]

432
00:25:03,524 --> 00:25:06,235
[Seongwon] <i>I had a feeling</i>
<i>this day would come.</i>

433
00:25:06,902 --> 00:25:09,154
From the first day I met you.

434
00:25:10,489 --> 00:25:11,698
Think back carefully.

435
00:25:12,533 --> 00:25:16,120
Remember how good it felt
when you stabbed Younghwan.

436
00:25:16,620 --> 00:25:17,913
[bang]

437
00:25:17,996 --> 00:25:19,456
Don't run away from this.

438
00:25:19,540 --> 00:25:22,876
Once you accept it,
you'll finally be free.

439
00:25:24,503 --> 00:25:28,298
After all, you're my Little Prince.

440
00:25:29,925 --> 00:25:31,343
It was to awaken me.

441
00:25:33,095 --> 00:25:36,390
Yu Seongwon thinks I'm just like him.

442
00:25:37,266 --> 00:25:38,267
That I'm

443
00:25:39,059 --> 00:25:40,894
suppressing the urge to kill.

444
00:25:43,188 --> 00:25:45,440
So he wanted to turn me
into a murderer like him.

445
00:25:45,524 --> 00:25:47,025
[♪ music increases in tempo]

446
00:25:49,194 --> 00:25:50,237
[scoffs]

447
00:25:50,904 --> 00:25:51,905
[♪ music resumes tempo]

448
00:25:51,989 --> 00:25:53,448
[grunts, groans]

449
00:25:55,617 --> 00:25:56,743
[keyboard clacking]

450
00:25:58,453 --> 00:26:00,247
[grunting, coughs]

451
00:26:02,082 --> 00:26:03,125
Son of a...

452
00:26:03,208 --> 00:26:05,252
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

453
00:26:06,712 --> 00:26:07,838
[keys jingling]

454
00:26:08,755 --> 00:26:09,965
[latch clanks]

455
00:26:13,343 --> 00:26:15,762
-[touch-tones beeping]
-[guard] A detainee collapsed.

456
00:26:15,846 --> 00:26:17,306
Please call an ambulance.

457
00:26:17,389 --> 00:26:19,057
[grunts, choking]

458
00:26:19,808 --> 00:26:21,518
Cho Pilgu collapsed!

459
00:26:21,602 --> 00:26:23,353
[♪ music swells]

460
00:26:29,776 --> 00:26:30,777
[♪ music fades]

461
00:26:30,861 --> 00:26:32,988
-[siren blaring]
-[camera shutters clicking]

462
00:26:33,071 --> 00:26:34,740
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

463
00:26:41,788 --> 00:26:42,789
What happened?

464
00:26:43,832 --> 00:26:45,459
It's an acute drug overdose.

465
00:26:48,462 --> 00:26:49,963
That lawyer who came earlier.

466
00:26:50,047 --> 00:26:51,715
I'm Mr. Cho Pilgu's lawyer.

467
00:26:53,383 --> 00:26:55,510
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

468
00:26:59,598 --> 00:27:00,641
[tires screech]

469
00:27:04,686 --> 00:27:05,687
[♪ music swells]

470
00:27:11,526 --> 00:27:12,778
ATTORNEY SONG YEONWOO

471
00:27:13,820 --> 00:27:15,447
[♪ music resumes tempo]

472
00:27:15,530 --> 00:27:17,115
How can I help you?

473
00:27:17,199 --> 00:27:19,534
Are you Attorney Song Yeonwoo?

474
00:27:19,618 --> 00:27:22,537
Yes, I'm Song Yeonwoo.

475
00:27:22,621 --> 00:27:23,705
[sighs heavily]

476
00:27:24,331 --> 00:27:25,666
[sighs softly]

477
00:27:27,417 --> 00:27:28,460
[Junyoung sighs heavily]

478
00:27:31,463 --> 00:27:32,798
He's been dealt with.

479
00:27:33,423 --> 00:27:35,133
They won't find out who I am,

480
00:27:36,426 --> 00:27:37,636
but I'll lie low for now.

481
00:27:38,637 --> 00:27:39,888
You should delete me

482
00:27:41,223 --> 00:27:42,391
from the company's records.

483
00:27:55,737 --> 00:27:56,738
Well done.

484
00:27:57,406 --> 00:27:58,657
[♪ music swells]

485
00:28:04,538 --> 00:28:05,706
[♪ music fades]

486
00:28:09,876 --> 00:28:11,253
[breathes deeply]

487
00:28:11,336 --> 00:28:12,337
[sighs softly]

488
00:28:18,218 --> 00:28:19,928
[Byungsik sighs wearily]

489
00:28:20,012 --> 00:28:21,430
This doesn't look good.

490
00:28:23,098 --> 00:28:24,099
How did this happen?

491
00:28:25,183 --> 00:28:27,227
A suspect dying in police custody?

492
00:28:28,562 --> 00:28:31,690
It looks like someone impersonated
a lawyer and drugged him.

493
00:28:31,773 --> 00:28:34,234
Who? Did you find out who it was?

494
00:28:34,860 --> 00:28:36,611
-No, not yet.
-Hey!

495
00:28:37,237 --> 00:28:38,780
Are you trying to ruin me?

496
00:28:38,864 --> 00:28:40,323
You idiots!

497
00:28:40,407 --> 00:28:43,785
After all your fooling around,
this is what you come back with?

498
00:28:43,869 --> 00:28:46,455
Who's going to answer for this?

499
00:28:46,538 --> 00:28:47,831
Tell me, who?

500
00:28:50,500 --> 00:28:53,128
-We'll make sure--
-Hey! You're seriously...

501
00:28:53,712 --> 00:28:54,838
You.

502
00:28:54,921 --> 00:28:56,590
You caused all of this.

503
00:28:57,174 --> 00:28:58,717
Try to say another word.

504
00:28:58,800 --> 00:29:01,553
I'll fire you on the spot!

505
00:29:02,220 --> 00:29:03,430
Goddamn it!

506
00:29:04,056 --> 00:29:05,098
[grunts angrily]

507
00:29:05,182 --> 00:29:06,600
[♪ tense, pulsating music playing]

508
00:29:09,019 --> 00:29:10,854
[camera shutter clicking]

509
00:29:11,438 --> 00:29:12,439
[sighs softly]

510
00:29:15,650 --> 00:29:17,444
The incident at Detective Jin Isoo's--

511
00:29:17,527 --> 00:29:19,905
Is it true that the suspect
of this case has died?

512
00:29:20,739 --> 00:29:22,074
Yes, it's true.

513
00:29:22,157 --> 00:29:24,076
How did they die in police custody?

514
00:29:24,159 --> 00:29:27,370
We're still investigating that matter.

515
00:29:27,454 --> 00:29:30,457
Is it true that the killer impersonated
a lawyer and poisoned him?

516
00:29:30,540 --> 00:29:31,833
[reporters clamoring]

517
00:29:41,593 --> 00:29:43,136
[♪ music swells]

518
00:29:49,851 --> 00:29:54,064
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

519
00:29:54,147 --> 00:29:55,232
[♪ music fades]

520
00:30:02,781 --> 00:30:03,782
[exhales heavily]

521
00:30:04,491 --> 00:30:06,660
I'm starving. Let's get something to eat.

522
00:30:08,995 --> 00:30:12,958
Let's eat, then think about
how we'll catch Yu Seongwon.

523
00:30:13,041 --> 00:30:14,793
[♪ suspenseful, pulsating music playing]

524
00:30:14,876 --> 00:30:16,711
This might be an opportunity.

525
00:30:18,130 --> 00:30:20,632
If we can prove
Yu Seongwon orchestrated the murder,

526
00:30:21,550 --> 00:30:24,469
we can catch him
before he kills anyone else.

527
00:30:26,221 --> 00:30:28,265
Yu Seongwon went to UBS's main office.

528
00:30:29,683 --> 00:30:32,310
Minjae was following him
the day before Cho Pilgu died.

529
00:30:35,230 --> 00:30:38,567
Maybe he met Jeong Taeseon that day
and asked for her help.

530
00:30:39,860 --> 00:30:42,028
And Jeong Taeseon pulled something?

531
00:30:42,112 --> 00:30:43,280
Yes.

532
00:30:43,864 --> 00:30:47,325
[inhales sharply] There wasn't much time,
so it could be someone close to her.

533
00:30:49,369 --> 00:30:50,412
[sighs heavily]

534
00:30:52,247 --> 00:30:54,332
[line connects, ringing]

535
00:30:54,416 --> 00:30:55,667
[automated voice]
<i>The number you have dialed...</i>

536
00:30:55,750 --> 00:30:57,460
[sighs in exasperation]
Why won't he answer his phone?

537
00:30:57,544 --> 00:30:58,587
[line disconnects]

538
00:30:58,670 --> 00:31:00,255
[♪ music swells]

539
00:31:00,338 --> 00:31:01,464
[sighs heavily]

540
00:31:03,466 --> 00:31:04,593
[♪ music fades]

541
00:31:04,676 --> 00:31:05,802
Ms. Joo Hyera?

542
00:31:06,595 --> 00:31:07,846
Yes?

543
00:31:18,023 --> 00:31:20,108
[delivery agent]
We have a delivery for you.

544
00:31:20,192 --> 00:31:21,943
[delivery agents grunting]

545
00:31:24,487 --> 00:31:25,780
[delivery agent dusts hands]

546
00:31:29,326 --> 00:31:31,369
GANGHA POLICE STATION
DETECTIVE JOO HYERA

547
00:31:34,164 --> 00:31:35,290
[door opens]

548
00:31:37,584 --> 00:31:39,628
-What's that?
-Pass me a box cutter.

549
00:31:39,711 --> 00:31:40,754
[door closes]

550
00:31:41,421 --> 00:31:43,673
-[box cutter clicking]
-[tape slicing, ripping]

551
00:31:50,764 --> 00:31:52,182
[♪ tense, ominous music playing]

552
00:32:01,399 --> 00:32:03,151
[♪ suspenseful sting plays]

553
00:32:07,364 --> 00:32:08,406
[gasps softly]

554
00:32:09,783 --> 00:32:11,201
[Hyera exhales in disbelief]

555
00:32:11,284 --> 00:32:12,285
[whimpers]

556
00:32:12,369 --> 00:32:14,454
[breath trembling]

557
00:32:14,537 --> 00:32:15,914
Stop those delivery guys.

558
00:32:15,997 --> 00:32:17,249
Got it.

559
00:32:18,750 --> 00:32:20,001
[gasps, sobbing]

560
00:32:20,085 --> 00:32:21,378
[♪ music swells]

561
00:32:26,341 --> 00:32:27,342
Min...

562
00:32:30,887 --> 00:32:31,972
[♪ music fades]

563
00:32:34,057 --> 00:32:36,017
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

564
00:32:37,894 --> 00:32:39,396
[camera shutter clicking]

565
00:33:00,125 --> 00:33:02,002
[♪ music swells, fades]

566
00:33:02,085 --> 00:33:03,586
There was a body inside?

567
00:33:03,670 --> 00:33:05,255
We really don't know anything.

568
00:33:06,214 --> 00:33:07,590
Where did you get it from?

569
00:33:07,674 --> 00:33:09,551
[stutters] Namgye-dong.

570
00:33:09,634 --> 00:33:12,137
But that place is a redevelopment area,

571
00:33:12,220 --> 00:33:14,097
so everything's been cleared out.

572
00:33:14,180 --> 00:33:16,224
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

573
00:33:16,308 --> 00:33:18,727
<i>We were asked to move</i>
<i>something they left behind.</i>

574
00:33:19,352 --> 00:33:21,271
<i>They said the money was on top of the box.</i>

575
00:33:22,105 --> 00:33:23,773
[gasps] Jesus Christ.

576
00:33:26,151 --> 00:33:28,069
So you don't know
who commissioned the job?

577
00:33:28,695 --> 00:33:30,530
We did get a call,

578
00:33:31,489 --> 00:33:34,492
but when I tried the number just now,
the phone was off.

579
00:33:35,118 --> 00:33:36,119
You don't know their name?

580
00:33:36,661 --> 00:33:37,662
No.

581
00:33:38,413 --> 00:33:39,956
We didn't catch the name.

582
00:33:41,791 --> 00:33:44,461
You transported something
without knowing who hired you?

583
00:33:45,378 --> 00:33:47,213
We've barely had any work recently.

584
00:33:49,341 --> 00:33:52,010
And two million won is a lot of money.

585
00:33:56,139 --> 00:33:57,140
[sighs softly]

586
00:33:59,100 --> 00:34:01,227
[breathing heavily] You damn fool!

587
00:34:01,311 --> 00:34:02,687
What the hell happened?

588
00:34:02,771 --> 00:34:04,272
How did we get a body delivered?

589
00:34:04,356 --> 00:34:05,857
You're all out of your damn minds!

590
00:34:06,524 --> 00:34:08,318
Joo Hyera. Where the hell is Joo Hyera?

591
00:34:10,362 --> 00:34:11,571
Let go of me!

592
00:34:11,654 --> 00:34:13,531
[♪ gentle, melancholy music playing]

593
00:34:13,615 --> 00:34:15,283
[Taegyun panting softly]

594
00:34:18,453 --> 00:34:19,704
Sir. [sighs softly]

595
00:34:20,663 --> 00:34:21,664
For now,

596
00:34:22,999 --> 00:34:24,000
please just stay put.

597
00:34:24,084 --> 00:34:25,335
What?

598
00:34:25,919 --> 00:34:26,961
The person who died

599
00:34:28,171 --> 00:34:29,631
was Joo Hyera's junior officer.

600
00:34:31,049 --> 00:34:32,717
He used to work for me, too.

601
00:34:33,510 --> 00:34:34,636
[sighs softly]

602
00:34:34,719 --> 00:34:37,722
I'll face disciplinary action,
or even resign if I have to,

603
00:34:39,015 --> 00:34:40,016
so for now,

604
00:34:41,601 --> 00:34:43,019
please don't say anything.

605
00:34:46,731 --> 00:34:47,774
Please.

606
00:34:48,566 --> 00:34:49,818
[Taegyun sighs softly]

607
00:34:52,821 --> 00:34:54,489
[sniffles, crying]

608
00:34:54,572 --> 00:34:55,698
[sighs deeply]

609
00:34:59,744 --> 00:35:01,538
[gasps softly, breath trembling]

610
00:35:03,123 --> 00:35:04,207
[sighs deeply]

611
00:35:05,709 --> 00:35:06,835
[exhales heavily]

612
00:35:16,261 --> 00:35:17,262
[Changun] So it was Minjae.

613
00:35:20,306 --> 00:35:21,307
Was Minjae the one

614
00:35:22,434 --> 00:35:24,018
keeping an eye on Yu Seongwon?

615
00:35:26,271 --> 00:35:27,480
[voice shaking] Minjae was

616
00:35:28,773 --> 00:35:30,066
following Yu Seongwon.

617
00:35:32,360 --> 00:35:33,903
I lost contact with him after that.

618
00:35:37,240 --> 00:35:38,992
I didn't think anything of it.

619
00:35:40,660 --> 00:35:42,162
[breath trembling]

620
00:35:43,121 --> 00:35:44,456
[crying] I just waited.

621
00:35:48,293 --> 00:35:50,336
[gasps softly, breath trembling]

622
00:35:54,883 --> 00:35:56,009
[sighs deeply]

623
00:35:58,136 --> 00:35:59,304
[sniffles]

624
00:35:59,971 --> 00:36:00,972
[voice shaking] Did they find anything?

625
00:36:03,016 --> 00:36:04,309
Not yet.

626
00:36:06,311 --> 00:36:07,771
Let's give it some time.

627
00:36:08,646 --> 00:36:11,441
If we search thoroughly,
I'm sure we'll find something.

628
00:36:11,524 --> 00:36:12,692
No.

629
00:36:14,611 --> 00:36:15,987
We won't find anything.

630
00:36:17,906 --> 00:36:19,032
You know.

631
00:36:20,950 --> 00:36:22,452
You know what Yu Seongwon is like.

632
00:36:29,459 --> 00:36:30,460
Hyera.

633
00:36:31,628 --> 00:36:32,670
Hey, Joo Hyera.

634
00:36:32,754 --> 00:36:33,922
[♪ music fades]

635
00:36:36,299 --> 00:36:38,218
Did you find anything of note?

636
00:36:38,301 --> 00:36:40,637
[KCSI officer] Nothing in particular.
We'll go upstairs and check.

637
00:36:41,221 --> 00:36:42,555
[engine accelerating]

638
00:36:42,639 --> 00:36:44,224
[♪ suspenseful, foreboding music playing]

639
00:36:51,439 --> 00:36:52,482
[Isoo] How did it go?

640
00:36:53,066 --> 00:36:56,569
The truck doesn't seem related.
Forensics didn't find anything.

641
00:36:58,071 --> 00:37:00,073
[sighs in exasperation]
How on earth did this happen?

642
00:37:00,698 --> 00:37:02,116
And who's the person who died?

643
00:37:02,200 --> 00:37:03,952
His name is Jeong Minjae.

644
00:37:04,577 --> 00:37:05,703
Detective Joo's old colleague.

645
00:37:05,787 --> 00:37:06,996
What?

646
00:37:07,080 --> 00:37:08,665
What colleague...

647
00:37:10,333 --> 00:37:11,543
You mean he's a police officer?

648
00:37:12,502 --> 00:37:13,670
Not anymore.

649
00:37:14,796 --> 00:37:17,924
They picked up the box from here,
so go with Forensics to check it out.

650
00:37:18,675 --> 00:37:19,801
Okay.

651
00:37:21,678 --> 00:37:22,762
Where's Detective Joo?

652
00:37:23,972 --> 00:37:25,223
She left in a hurry earlier.

653
00:37:26,599 --> 00:37:28,142
[♪ music increases in tempo]

654
00:37:34,774 --> 00:37:36,484
[engine accelerating]

655
00:37:40,321 --> 00:37:41,489
[♪ music fades]

656
00:37:44,492 --> 00:37:46,953
[♪ tense, ominous music playing]

657
00:37:47,745 --> 00:37:49,455
[footsteps approaching]

658
00:37:58,798 --> 00:38:01,217
-[loud, distant bang]
-[alarm blaring]

659
00:38:03,344 --> 00:38:04,804
[gate whirring]

660
00:38:08,516 --> 00:38:09,642
[engine revs]

661
00:38:12,186 --> 00:38:13,396
We have a guest.

662
00:38:14,105 --> 00:38:15,106
Go and see.

663
00:38:15,189 --> 00:38:17,275
[♪ foreboding, pulsating music playing]

664
00:38:25,783 --> 00:38:27,160
Yu Seongwon is inside, isn't he?

665
00:38:38,504 --> 00:38:40,048
Detective Joo Hyera.

666
00:38:40,131 --> 00:38:41,382
Long time no see.

667
00:38:41,466 --> 00:38:42,884
Why did you kill him?

668
00:38:43,676 --> 00:38:44,677
What?

669
00:38:45,470 --> 00:38:46,971
Why did you kill him?

670
00:38:48,222 --> 00:38:49,432
Hey!

671
00:38:50,099 --> 00:38:51,100
Let go.

672
00:38:55,188 --> 00:38:57,982
Leave. She's my guest.

673
00:39:03,196 --> 00:39:06,199
I'm so sorry. He doesn't have any manners.
[chuckles]

674
00:39:07,241 --> 00:39:08,493
Anyway,

675
00:39:09,577 --> 00:39:10,787
did someone die?

676
00:39:10,870 --> 00:39:11,955
[♪ music swells]

677
00:39:14,415 --> 00:39:15,583
[♪ music fades]

678
00:39:17,710 --> 00:39:19,671
You think you're perfect, don't you?

679
00:39:20,296 --> 00:39:21,756
[♪ suspenseful, foreboding music playing]

680
00:39:21,839 --> 00:39:23,383
You think after killing five people,

681
00:39:24,175 --> 00:39:26,344
you didn't leave
a single trace, don't you?

682
00:39:27,345 --> 00:39:28,388
[scoffs]

683
00:39:29,305 --> 00:39:31,265
But you left a long trail this time.

684
00:39:32,183 --> 00:39:34,060
You moved the body,

685
00:39:34,727 --> 00:39:35,937
called a truck,

686
00:39:37,188 --> 00:39:38,523
and sent it to me.

687
00:39:40,984 --> 00:39:42,235
Why did you go that far?

688
00:39:44,821 --> 00:39:46,114
Am I starting to scare you?

689
00:39:48,408 --> 00:39:50,201
Are you finally afraid
you might get caught?

690
00:39:50,284 --> 00:39:51,327
[scoffs]

691
00:39:51,703 --> 00:39:52,954
Unbelievable.

692
00:40:02,380 --> 00:40:03,673
[Seongwon] Everyone

693
00:40:04,924 --> 00:40:06,551
asks me why.

694
00:40:06,634 --> 00:40:09,554
"Why? Why on earth?"

695
00:40:09,637 --> 00:40:12,306
As if they could understand
if I told them.

696
00:40:12,390 --> 00:40:13,641
But the thing is,

697
00:40:15,476 --> 00:40:17,895
there is no answer to begin with.

698
00:40:20,523 --> 00:40:21,524
I am...

699
00:40:23,484 --> 00:40:26,946
beyond the understanding
of someone like you.

700
00:40:27,030 --> 00:40:28,031
You're right.

701
00:40:30,658 --> 00:40:32,952
I treated you like a person,

702
00:40:33,870 --> 00:40:35,663
when you're not even human.

703
00:40:39,834 --> 00:40:41,669
I'm working on a new piece.

704
00:40:42,378 --> 00:40:43,379
Would you like to see?

705
00:40:52,555 --> 00:40:54,182
[♪ ominous sting plays]

706
00:40:54,265 --> 00:40:55,683
[breath trembling]

707
00:40:58,478 --> 00:40:59,812
[♪ music fades]

708
00:41:02,940 --> 00:41:05,109
[♪ gentle, poignant music playing]

709
00:41:07,236 --> 00:41:10,073
Hey, I told you to stop coming.

710
00:41:10,156 --> 00:41:12,366
I wouldn't have to come
if you had a girlfriend.

711
00:41:13,451 --> 00:41:15,036
You didn't like the hospital food.

712
00:41:15,119 --> 00:41:18,748
Oh, I can't resist fried chicken.
[chuckles softly]

713
00:41:24,378 --> 00:41:25,421
[chuckles]

714
00:41:31,177 --> 00:41:32,428
Here.

715
00:41:37,683 --> 00:41:40,103
Hey, I told you
not to look at me like that.

716
00:41:40,812 --> 00:41:42,522
What do you mean? Like what?

717
00:41:42,605 --> 00:41:45,566
It was my mistake that got me stabbed,

718
00:41:45,650 --> 00:41:46,692
so stop doing that.

719
00:41:48,528 --> 00:41:51,197
[inhales deeply]
Your mistake is my mistake, too.

720
00:41:51,989 --> 00:41:53,282
Seriously!

721
00:41:54,367 --> 00:41:56,828
Fine, I'll stop.

722
00:41:57,411 --> 00:41:58,412
Just eat up.

723
00:41:59,622 --> 00:42:00,748
[chuckles]

724
00:42:02,291 --> 00:42:04,252
-Is it good?
-[both chuckle]

725
00:42:04,877 --> 00:42:06,712
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

726
00:42:06,796 --> 00:42:08,214
[breath trembling]

727
00:42:15,012 --> 00:42:16,597
[breathing shakily]

728
00:42:20,977 --> 00:42:22,979
Are you that touched?

729
00:42:24,105 --> 00:42:25,565
[breathing shakily]

730
00:42:28,693 --> 00:42:29,819
[grunts]

731
00:42:29,944 --> 00:42:31,320
[Isoo] Detective Joo!

732
00:42:31,404 --> 00:42:32,446
[grunts]

733
00:42:32,530 --> 00:42:33,739
[Hyera crying]

734
00:42:40,788 --> 00:42:43,207
Jeez. Isoo!

735
00:42:43,291 --> 00:42:45,418
She's out of control right now.

736
00:42:45,501 --> 00:42:47,378
[Hyera panting, breath trembling]

737
00:42:49,881 --> 00:42:51,549
Are you going to trust someone like her?

738
00:42:51,632 --> 00:42:53,259
You shut your mouth.

739
00:42:57,889 --> 00:42:59,140
[scoffs, mutters]

740
00:42:59,223 --> 00:43:00,892
[breathing heavily]

741
00:43:10,860 --> 00:43:11,986
[♪ music fades]

742
00:43:13,654 --> 00:43:15,823
It's possible he was murdered here.

743
00:43:15,907 --> 00:43:17,617
-We need to find traces of blood.
-[KCSI officers] Okay.

744
00:43:17,700 --> 00:43:19,952
[♪ suspenseful, pulsating music playing]

745
00:43:30,046 --> 00:43:31,380
[camera shutter clicking]

746
00:43:46,646 --> 00:43:47,772
[♪ music fades]

747
00:43:52,401 --> 00:43:53,903
[line connects, ringing]

748
00:43:56,614 --> 00:43:58,574
[♪ somber, melancholy music playing]

749
00:43:59,158 --> 00:44:00,493
[sighs softly]

750
00:44:00,576 --> 00:44:02,578
-[sighs wearily]
-[cell phone vibrating]

751
00:44:07,708 --> 00:44:09,835
Yeah. Did you find anything?

752
00:44:09,961 --> 00:44:11,295
[Junyoung] <i>No. </i>[sighs]

753
00:44:11,379 --> 00:44:13,297
There's no trace of blood anywhere.

754
00:44:13,923 --> 00:44:15,758
This might not be where he was killed.

755
00:44:18,844 --> 00:44:20,054
[cell phone snaps shut]

756
00:44:28,396 --> 00:44:29,647
[line connects, ringing]

757
00:44:31,774 --> 00:44:33,484
-[line clicks]
-Yes, Dr. Yoon.

758
00:44:34,819 --> 00:44:36,279
Did you look at the body?

759
00:44:36,362 --> 00:44:39,073
It looks like they used a stun gun.

760
00:44:39,156 --> 00:44:41,450
There's an indentation
in the back of his head,

761
00:44:42,410 --> 00:44:45,538
and there are bruises all over his body.

762
00:44:46,289 --> 00:44:47,665
[sighs deeply]

763
00:44:48,791 --> 00:44:49,959
[exhales softly]

764
00:44:54,130 --> 00:44:55,339
Should I go in alone?

765
00:44:56,299 --> 00:44:57,425
[exhales]

766
00:44:57,925 --> 00:44:59,176
No, let's go together.

767
00:45:04,724 --> 00:45:05,891
[♪ music fades]

768
00:45:06,559 --> 00:45:08,686
At 11:00 p.m. on Sunday,

769
00:45:08,769 --> 00:45:10,354
you went to UBS's main office.

770
00:45:11,605 --> 00:45:12,606
Why?

771
00:45:15,109 --> 00:45:16,777
Tell us what you did after that.

772
00:45:17,278 --> 00:45:18,362
[sighs in exasperation]

773
00:45:18,446 --> 00:45:20,323
This is seriously no fun. [clicks tongue]

774
00:45:21,657 --> 00:45:23,326
[♪ somber, suspenseful music playing]

775
00:45:23,409 --> 00:45:24,785
[breathes deeply]

776
00:45:26,454 --> 00:45:27,455
Isoo.

777
00:45:28,331 --> 00:45:29,749
What are you doing?

778
00:45:30,624 --> 00:45:32,668
Why do you keep pretending you're normal?

779
00:45:33,252 --> 00:45:35,171
Are you going to
keep asking dumb questions?

780
00:45:35,254 --> 00:45:37,381
How long do I have to keep
opening your eyes?

781
00:45:38,841 --> 00:45:39,842
Right.

782
00:45:41,969 --> 00:45:43,804
That's why you killed Younghwan.

783
00:45:44,889 --> 00:45:47,391
Because you thought we were alike.

784
00:45:49,477 --> 00:45:50,853
You said you grew up lonely.

785
00:45:51,729 --> 00:45:53,230
That you felt abandoned.

786
00:45:54,273 --> 00:45:57,026
You assumed we were the same
and got the wrong idea.

787
00:45:59,195 --> 00:46:00,196
I'm not like you.

788
00:46:02,156 --> 00:46:03,157
I had...

789
00:46:07,286 --> 00:46:09,163
a mother who cherished me.

790
00:46:09,246 --> 00:46:10,748
[♪ music turns ominous]

791
00:46:12,917 --> 00:46:14,794
You didn't have a mother like that.

792
00:46:14,877 --> 00:46:17,296
That's why you ended up completely broken.

793
00:46:17,963 --> 00:46:19,673
You were damaged beyond repair.

794
00:46:22,676 --> 00:46:25,388
After Kim Younghwan died
and Cho Pilgu was caught,

795
00:46:25,471 --> 00:46:27,515
did you feel scared and run to your mom?

796
00:46:28,182 --> 00:46:29,767
Did you beg her for help?

797
00:46:29,850 --> 00:46:31,769
From the mom who despises you?

798
00:46:31,852 --> 00:46:33,354
[♪ music increases in tempo]

799
00:46:34,480 --> 00:46:35,648
[scoffs softly]

800
00:46:38,317 --> 00:46:39,360
[♪ music fades]

801
00:46:50,871 --> 00:46:52,623
[♪ tense, ominous music playing]

802
00:47:02,925 --> 00:47:04,969
Hey, isn't that Chairwoman Jeong Taeseon?

803
00:47:05,553 --> 00:47:06,595
I think it is.

804
00:47:06,679 --> 00:47:07,888
[♪ music swells]

805
00:47:10,766 --> 00:47:11,892
[♪ music fades]

806
00:47:13,394 --> 00:47:16,897
We're looking for the man
who impersonated a lawyer.

807
00:47:17,815 --> 00:47:21,277
We're also combing through the place
where you disposed of the body.

808
00:47:22,027 --> 00:47:24,113
We'll pull footage
from every camera nearby.

809
00:47:24,196 --> 00:47:26,157
[♪ gripping, ominous music playing]

810
00:47:26,240 --> 00:47:27,908
[sighs deeply]

811
00:47:31,954 --> 00:47:33,372
I'm going to catch you in the end.

812
00:47:35,875 --> 00:47:39,086
Save yourself the humiliation
of being dragged in and just confess.

813
00:47:39,795 --> 00:47:41,172
[sighs, scoffs]

814
00:47:41,255 --> 00:47:43,090
[laughing smugly]

815
00:47:44,300 --> 00:47:48,137
Why do you keep saying I killed someone?

816
00:47:49,138 --> 00:47:51,182
Why would I kill him?

817
00:47:51,807 --> 00:47:52,808
I mean,

818
00:47:54,018 --> 00:47:55,019
did he follow me...

819
00:47:58,189 --> 00:47:59,648
and spy on me or something?

820
00:47:59,732 --> 00:48:02,818
Because of his foolish superior
who thinks I'm a murderer?

821
00:48:06,447 --> 00:48:08,199
Unless that's what pissed me off,

822
00:48:08,282 --> 00:48:10,743
there's no reason for me to kill him.

823
00:48:14,205 --> 00:48:15,206
Oh.

824
00:48:16,040 --> 00:48:17,041
Right there.

825
00:48:18,042 --> 00:48:19,293
That's a great expression.

826
00:48:21,420 --> 00:48:22,421
Want to be my model?

827
00:48:25,382 --> 00:48:26,800
[exhales sharply]

828
00:48:31,347 --> 00:48:32,681
[♪ music fades]

829
00:48:34,058 --> 00:48:36,894
Mr. Yu Seongwon, please get up.

830
00:48:39,772 --> 00:48:41,190
[Seongwon sighs contentedly]

831
00:48:41,273 --> 00:48:43,150
-Sir.
-Be quiet.

832
00:48:44,193 --> 00:48:45,277
[scoffs softly]

833
00:48:48,864 --> 00:48:50,950
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

834
00:49:20,187 --> 00:49:21,313
[door closes]

835
00:49:28,612 --> 00:49:29,697
[Hyera] Wait!

836
00:49:29,780 --> 00:49:31,031
[Hyera panting]

837
00:49:33,867 --> 00:49:35,160
Your son is a murderer.

838
00:49:38,831 --> 00:49:40,124
He killed five people.

839
00:49:47,715 --> 00:49:48,841
You know, don't you?

840
00:49:50,801 --> 00:49:51,802
You're his mother.

841
00:49:52,720 --> 00:49:53,971
Of course, you know.

842
00:49:56,181 --> 00:49:58,183
He's going to continue killing people.

843
00:49:59,393 --> 00:50:01,228
This isn't something you can cover up.

844
00:50:04,857 --> 00:50:06,150
You have no manners.

845
00:50:07,109 --> 00:50:08,569
And have no fear.

846
00:50:09,653 --> 00:50:11,614
People like that
usually come to a bad end.

847
00:50:14,617 --> 00:50:15,868
You should be careful.

848
00:50:24,960 --> 00:50:25,961
[car door closes]

849
00:50:27,713 --> 00:50:28,964
[♪ music swells]

850
00:50:40,476 --> 00:50:41,560
[♪ music fades]

851
00:50:41,644 --> 00:50:43,937
Keep your subordinates in line!

852
00:50:44,605 --> 00:50:45,606
Yes, sir.

853
00:50:45,689 --> 00:50:47,191
For Christ's sake.

854
00:50:53,822 --> 00:50:55,449
From now on,

855
00:50:56,367 --> 00:50:57,743
this case goes to Team 2!

856
00:50:57,826 --> 00:50:59,870
[♪ somber, suspenseful music playing]

857
00:50:59,953 --> 00:51:01,622
-You can't.
-I can't?

858
00:51:01,705 --> 00:51:03,874
-I've been too patient with you.
-Sir.

859
00:51:07,503 --> 00:51:08,545
[scoffs softly]

860
00:51:09,838 --> 00:51:12,299
I heard the victim was
your junior officer.

861
00:51:12,383 --> 00:51:13,759
Huh?

862
00:51:13,842 --> 00:51:16,929
Can an involved party
be in charge of a case?

863
00:51:19,431 --> 00:51:20,641
I'm the one

864
00:51:21,892 --> 00:51:23,352
who knows this case best.

865
00:51:24,687 --> 00:51:26,230
Yu Seongwon is the killer.

866
00:51:28,065 --> 00:51:29,108
Do you have evidence?

867
00:51:29,191 --> 00:51:30,401
I'm going to find it.

868
00:51:30,984 --> 00:51:33,696
[scoffs] Isn't it all just in your head?

869
00:51:33,779 --> 00:51:37,157
You've invented a whole story,
and you're twisting everything to fit.

870
00:51:37,241 --> 00:51:38,242
No, I'm not.

871
00:51:39,118 --> 00:51:40,119
Yu Seongwon

872
00:51:41,203 --> 00:51:43,330
has been killing people continuously.

873
00:51:44,998 --> 00:51:48,627
You're out of your mind. [exclaims]

874
00:51:48,711 --> 00:51:50,629
Stay out of this investigation!

875
00:51:50,713 --> 00:51:52,506
-Sir.
-Chief Park.

876
00:51:53,424 --> 00:51:56,677
The body of Joo Hyera's junior officer
was delivered to her.

877
00:51:56,760 --> 00:52:01,557
Can she stay on this case?

878
00:52:06,019 --> 00:52:07,104
She can't.

879
00:52:07,187 --> 00:52:08,731
[♪ music increases in tempo]

880
00:52:15,571 --> 00:52:16,572
Team 2!

881
00:52:16,655 --> 00:52:18,699
Don't spin some story like she did.

882
00:52:18,782 --> 00:52:21,201
Find the real killer, got it?

883
00:52:21,285 --> 00:52:22,327
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

884
00:52:23,120 --> 00:52:25,164
Damn it.

885
00:52:27,499 --> 00:52:28,584
[door closes]

886
00:52:29,668 --> 00:52:30,836
[♪ music fades]

887
00:52:35,799 --> 00:52:37,134
Leave the country right now.

888
00:52:37,843 --> 00:52:39,261
I told you I have an exhibition.

889
00:52:39,344 --> 00:52:41,430
Must I really go through this
because of you?

890
00:52:46,602 --> 00:52:47,978
[inhales sharply]

891
00:52:48,061 --> 00:52:51,440
I think we'll have to kill
that boyfriend of yours.

892
00:52:53,317 --> 00:52:54,902
-What?
-Why?

893
00:52:55,569 --> 00:52:56,570
Do you love him?

894
00:52:57,362 --> 00:52:58,363
[scoffs]

895
00:52:58,447 --> 00:53:00,157
You don't know anything about that.

896
00:53:00,240 --> 00:53:01,408
[sighs heavily]

897
00:53:04,745 --> 00:53:07,748
You had me because you wanted
to be the chairman's second wife.

898
00:53:08,957 --> 00:53:09,958
But

899
00:53:10,626 --> 00:53:12,127
even just a little,

900
00:53:14,797 --> 00:53:16,673
did you ever love me?

901
00:53:20,677 --> 00:53:22,721
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

902
00:53:22,805 --> 00:53:24,139
[breathes deeply]

903
00:53:25,098 --> 00:53:26,850
Isoo told me

904
00:53:26,934 --> 00:53:29,311
that I ended up broken because of you.

905
00:53:30,020 --> 00:53:31,563
So you should take responsibility.

906
00:53:31,647 --> 00:53:33,190
Leave the country for a while.

907
00:53:33,273 --> 00:53:35,108
The police have nothing on me.

908
00:53:35,192 --> 00:53:36,860
They don't have any evidence.

909
00:53:36,944 --> 00:53:39,112
Stay away until things settle down!

910
00:53:41,740 --> 00:53:43,033
[swears softly]

911
00:53:45,994 --> 00:53:48,831
Should I just come clean?

912
00:53:50,249 --> 00:53:53,502
Seeing you with your head down
and your hands cuffed,

913
00:53:54,086 --> 00:53:57,923
being dragged around,
while reporters take pictures of you...

914
00:53:58,006 --> 00:54:00,926
[laughing] ...might actually be quite fun.

915
00:54:03,595 --> 00:54:05,472
-Honestly.
-[♪ music fades]

916
00:54:06,306 --> 00:54:08,976
What do you mean
Yu Seongwon has been killing people?

917
00:54:09,059 --> 00:54:10,936
Are you saying he's a serial killer?

918
00:54:11,979 --> 00:54:12,980
Yes.

919
00:54:13,063 --> 00:54:14,356
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

920
00:54:14,439 --> 00:54:15,858
Two of Yu Seongwon's models

921
00:54:16,650 --> 00:54:18,360
and his underclassman are missing.

922
00:54:19,194 --> 00:54:20,320
Detective Joo thinks

923
00:54:21,154 --> 00:54:25,200
Yu Seongwon was inspired by his murders
and created these pieces.

924
00:54:25,284 --> 00:54:27,578
[♪ suspenseful, pulsating music playing]

925
00:54:29,413 --> 00:54:32,624
After Kim Heejun went missing,
Yu Seongwon left for the UK.

926
00:54:33,292 --> 00:54:35,085
He came back recently for an exhibition.

927
00:54:36,211 --> 00:54:37,713
Detective Joo moved back here

928
00:54:38,839 --> 00:54:40,173
to catch Yu Seongwon.

929
00:54:41,258 --> 00:54:42,593
To catch Yu Seongwon?

930
00:54:43,302 --> 00:54:45,596
Then what happened to Jeong Minjae?

931
00:54:46,597 --> 00:54:50,100
He was following Yu Seongwon,
and then we lost contact with him.

932
00:54:52,728 --> 00:54:54,021
[sighs deeply]

933
00:54:54,104 --> 00:54:56,273
Do you think
Yu Seongwon is the killer, too?

934
00:54:56,356 --> 00:54:58,692
Yes, I'm certain.

935
00:55:00,569 --> 00:55:03,030
He killed Younghwan to provoke me.

936
00:55:05,616 --> 00:55:07,743
But we don't have any evidence.

937
00:55:08,368 --> 00:55:09,536
[♪ music fades]

938
00:55:10,120 --> 00:55:11,496
These are old case files.

939
00:55:11,580 --> 00:55:13,832
Let's check them
to see if we've missed anything.

940
00:55:13,915 --> 00:55:15,334
-Okay.
-[sighs]

941
00:55:15,417 --> 00:55:17,127
[♪ gentle, melancholy music playing]

942
00:55:19,254 --> 00:55:20,505
[sighs in exasperation]

943
00:55:21,089 --> 00:55:23,175
[sniffles, sighs heavily]

944
00:55:23,258 --> 00:55:25,385
[breath trembling, sighing]

945
00:55:28,263 --> 00:55:29,264
Hyera.

946
00:55:29,348 --> 00:55:30,932
[Hyera sniffles, sighs]

947
00:55:32,225 --> 00:55:33,644
[exhales softly]

948
00:55:37,189 --> 00:55:38,315
I know how you feel.

949
00:55:38,398 --> 00:55:39,900
[breath trembling]

950
00:55:41,109 --> 00:55:42,569
[Changun]
Just pull yourself together first.

951
00:55:45,155 --> 00:55:46,573
We're going to catch Yu Seongwon.

952
00:55:47,324 --> 00:55:48,617
It may seem hopeless right now,

953
00:55:50,202 --> 00:55:51,703
but we'll catch him in the end.

954
00:55:51,787 --> 00:55:53,497
[breath continues trembling]

955
00:55:55,707 --> 00:55:57,042
[♪ music swells]

956
00:56:01,338 --> 00:56:02,547
[♪ music fades]

957
00:56:04,758 --> 00:56:06,468
[♪ gripping, ominous music playing]

958
00:56:12,015 --> 00:56:13,725
[Isoo] <i>You didn't have a mother like that.</i>

959
00:56:13,809 --> 00:56:15,852
That's why you ended up completely broken.

960
00:56:17,187 --> 00:56:18,897
You were damaged beyond repair.

961
00:56:18,980 --> 00:56:21,066
Did you feel scared and run to your mom?

962
00:56:22,359 --> 00:56:24,027
Did you beg her for help?

963
00:56:24,111 --> 00:56:26,029
From the mom who despises you?

964
00:56:26,613 --> 00:56:27,656
[sighs softly]

965
00:56:28,740 --> 00:56:29,825
[scoffs]

966
00:56:30,867 --> 00:56:32,119
[sighs wearily]

967
00:56:34,538 --> 00:56:35,914
[sighs deeply]

968
00:56:39,543 --> 00:56:40,919
[shattering]

969
00:56:41,628 --> 00:56:43,088
[breathing heavily]

970
00:56:45,507 --> 00:56:46,550
[clangs]

971
00:56:50,011 --> 00:56:51,763
[hurried footsteps approaching]

972
00:56:57,561 --> 00:56:58,729
[sighs softly]

973
00:57:05,694 --> 00:57:06,820
[groans softly]

974
00:57:06,903 --> 00:57:08,155
[♪ music increases in tempo]

975
00:57:08,739 --> 00:57:09,906
[inhales deeply]

976
00:57:12,909 --> 00:57:14,244
[exhales deeply]

977
00:57:14,327 --> 00:57:15,620
[♪ music swells]

978
00:57:21,334 --> 00:57:22,419
[sighs softly]

979
00:57:24,921 --> 00:57:25,964
[♪ music fades]

980
00:57:26,047 --> 00:57:28,633
TWO DAYS EARLIER

981
00:57:28,717 --> 00:57:30,635
[♪ suspenseful, ominous music playing]

982
00:57:40,687 --> 00:57:41,730
[scoffs]

983
00:57:41,813 --> 00:57:43,148
[♪ music increases in tempo]

984
00:58:45,210 --> 00:58:46,503
[♪ music swells]

985
00:58:47,629 --> 00:58:49,130
-[taser crackling]
-[heavy thud]

986
00:58:49,840 --> 00:58:51,216
[♪ music resumes tempo]

987
00:58:55,720 --> 00:58:57,931
[♪ tense, ominous music playing]

988
00:59:37,804 --> 00:59:41,558
[♪ ominous chord swells]

989
00:59:43,977 --> 00:59:45,353
[chuckles softly]

990
00:59:45,437 --> 00:59:47,564
[♪ melancholy piano music playing]

991
00:59:49,441 --> 00:59:50,567
[Mr. Hwang grunts]

992
00:59:58,867 --> 01:00:00,577
[flames roaring]

993
01:00:13,048 --> 01:00:14,591
[♪ music swells]

994
01:00:31,775 --> 01:00:32,859
[inhales sharply]

995
01:00:34,653 --> 01:00:35,779
[exhales deeply]

996
01:00:37,072 --> 01:00:38,114
[chuckles softly]

997
01:00:45,997 --> 01:00:47,165
[laughs maliciously]

998
01:00:54,756 --> 01:00:55,799
[♪ music fades]

999
01:00:55,882 --> 01:00:56,883
FLEX X COP 2
EPISODE 12

1000
01:00:56,967 --> 01:00:58,385
THE MADNESS IS FINALLY UNVEILED

1001
01:00:58,468 --> 01:00:59,928
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

1002
01:01:33,503 --> 01:01:35,171
What's Yu Seongwon's weakness?

1003
01:01:35,255 --> 01:01:36,339
Don't touch my son.

1004
01:01:36,423 --> 01:01:37,757
[Taegyun] <i>You're suspended as of now.</i>

1005
01:01:37,841 --> 01:01:38,925
[Isoo] <i>I'll resign.</i>

1006
01:01:39,009 --> 01:01:40,135
[Hyera] Jin Isoo!

1007
01:01:40,218 --> 01:01:42,095
[Isoo] <i>Detective Joo,</i>
<i>stay and hold the line.</i>

1008
01:01:42,178 --> 01:01:44,848
Hello! Watch how far I can go.

1009
01:01:44,931 --> 01:01:46,266
<i>They're even threatening to sue.</i>

1010
01:01:46,349 --> 01:01:47,934
I have a plane ready. Get out now.

1011
01:01:48,018 --> 01:01:49,644
Yu Seongwon's flying out in two hours.

1012
01:01:49,728 --> 01:01:50,812
<i>Just go and arrest him first.</i>

1013
01:01:50,895 --> 01:01:53,523
Now's the time to repay your debt.

1014
01:01:53,606 --> 01:01:55,442
<i>-</i>[tires screech]
<i>-</i>[Kyungjin] Pull over!

1015
01:01:56,109 --> 01:01:57,610
[man] <i>Jin Isoo is in the studio.</i>

1016
01:01:58,319 --> 01:01:59,404
Burn them all.

1017
01:02:00,822 --> 01:02:03,867
[Seongwon] <i>Do you really think</i>
<i>you can catch me?</i>

1018
01:02:07,078 --> 01:02:08,246
[♪ music fades]

1019
01:02:13,251 --> 01:02:14,627
[woman] <i>Mr. Yu, welcome.</i>

1020
01:02:14,711 --> 01:02:16,546
Hello.

1021
01:02:16,629 --> 01:02:19,507
Looking handsome as always.
How have you been?

1022
01:02:19,591 --> 01:02:21,342
Doing well. How about you, Director?

1023
01:02:21,926 --> 01:02:24,304
It's been frantic getting ready
for the exhibition.

1024
01:02:24,387 --> 01:02:26,389
This way, please.
I have the pieces all set up.

1025
01:02:34,731 --> 01:02:35,815
What do you think?

1026
01:02:38,693 --> 01:02:40,445
[♪ gripping, ominous music playing]

1027
01:02:42,197 --> 01:02:43,573
As for this exhibition...

1028
01:02:48,328 --> 01:02:49,996
That one is the centerpiece.

1029
01:02:52,707 --> 01:02:56,211
It should be the first thing people see
when they walk in.

1030
01:02:59,255 --> 01:03:02,342
It needs to feel real...

1031
01:03:03,134 --> 01:03:05,053
as if it were alive.

1032
01:03:07,472 --> 01:03:08,723
Understood?

1033
01:03:08,807 --> 01:03:10,809
Translated by Hyesoo Lee

